0.055}],"lens":"Williams lens (a tribute to Tom Williams's method): Background first: TGLS is in a downtrend, the VSA balance reads neutral (46/100), last key bar ETF on 10 Sep. Holmes strength sequence S1 (demand overcoming supply → no supply / test → no supply) completed 2 Oct: demand overcoming supply 28 Sep → no supply / test 1 Oct → no supply 2 Oct. It confirms on a trade above 35.99; a close below 34.02 proves it wrong (triggered). Desk backtest for S1: edge (+0.07R over 3362 trades). Holmes strength sequence S10 (reversal over two bars → no supply → no supply) completed 2 Oct: reversal over two bars 16 Sep → no supply 1 Oct → no supply 2 Oct. It confirms on a trade above 35.99; a close below 34.02 proves it wrong (triggered). Desk backtest for S10: edge (+0.11R over 1613 trades)."},"scores":{"overall":25,"group":"whole universe","group_rank":335,"group_n":388,"sector_rank":167,"sector_n":189,"earn":31}},"biz":{"name":"Tecnoglass Holdings Inc.","desc":"Tecnoglass Holdings Inc. manufactures, supplies, and installs architectural glass, windows, and aluminum and vinyl products for commercial and residential construction markets in Colombia, the United States, Panama, and internationally. The company offers low emissivity, laminated/thermo-laminated, thermo-acoustic, tempered, silk-screened, curved, and digital print glass products. It also provides aluminum products, including bars, plates, profiles, rods, and tubes for use in the manufacturing of architectural glass settings, such as windows, doors, spatial separators, and related products under the Alutions brand name. In addition, the company offers curtain wall/floating facades, stick facade systems, windows and doors, interior dividers and commercial display windows, and hurricane-proof windows; StormArmour, that are attachment for sliding doors, and other products, such as awnings, structures, and automatic doors; and other components of architectural systems. It markets and sells its products primarily under the Tecnoglass, ESWindows, Alutions, Energia Solar S.A, ES, ES Imagine Extraordinary, Eswindows, Tecnobend, Tecnoair, Tecnosmart, ECOMAX by ESWINDOWS, ESWINDOWS Interiors, ESW Windows and Walls, Solartec by Tecnoglass, Solar Windows, Componenti, ES Metals, and E-skin, Prestige by ESWINDOWS, Eli by ESWINDOWS, Alessia by ESWINDOWS, Elite Line by ESWindows, ULTRAVIEW by Tecnoglass, and MULTIMAX by ESWIDOWS brand names through internal and independent sales representatives, as well as directly to distributors. It serves developers, general contractors or installers for hotels, office buildings, shopping centers, airports, universities, hospitals, and multifamily and residential buildings. The company was formerly known as Tecnoglass Inc. and changed its name to Tecnoglass Holdings Inc. in July 2026. Tecnoglass Holdings Inc. was founded in 1983 and is based in Miami, Florida.","desc_src":"Yahoo Finance profile via yfinance (third-party)","sic":"3211","sic_desc":"Flat Glass","sector":"Basic Materials","industry":"Building Materials","mcap":1664560384,"mcap_src":"Yahoo Finance profile (third-party, cached)","hq":"MIAMI, FL","exchange":"XNYS","fy_end":"1231","cik":1534675,"state_inc":"E9","massive_note":"Massive ticker details not fetched yet (5 calls/min limit; filled in on a nightly run)","sec_asof":"2026-10-08"},"fin":{"available":true,"src":"SEC EDGAR XBRL companyfacts","asof":"2026-10-08","q":[{"end":"2023-09-30","rev":210743000.0,"rev_yoy":4.4,"eps":0.96,"eps_yoy":-2.0,"ni":45863000.0,"ni_yoy":-1.8,"nm":21.8,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2023-12-31","rev":194603000.0,"rev_yoy":-7.8,"eps":0.77,"eps_yoy":-33.0,"ni":36339000.0,"ni_yoy":-33.9,"nm":18.7,"derived":["eps","rev","ni"],"fp":null},{"end":"2024-03-31","rev":192627000.0,"rev_yoy":-4.9,"eps":0.63,"eps_yoy":-37.6,"ni":29730000.0,"ni_yoy":-38.4,"nm":15.4,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2024-06-30","rev":219654000.0,"rev_yoy":-2.5,"eps":0.75,"eps_yoy":-31.8,"ni":35028000.0,"ni_yoy":-33.2,"nm":15.9,"derived":